job_summary:
Job title: Senior FP&A Analyst
Package: Competitive
Location:
Bristol (hybrid working 2 days in the office)
Reporting to: Head of FP&A
Job type: Full Time
Our Client
Our client is an exciting high growth independent financial services business based in Bristol.
They are now seeking an experienced finance professional to support decision making and provide meaningful insight into their advisory business.
Our client is an equal opportunities employer, so if you’re just returning to work or need to work flexibly then we’d like to hear from you.
Senior FP&A Analyst - The Role
As Senior FP&A Analyst, you will gain an understanding of the key business drivers and metrics to create accurate reports with dashboards and insight-driven commentary.
Specifically, Your Role Will Include
Produce regular business performance reports on key performance indicators;
Provide analysis on profitability and trends to assist with SLT decision making and strategy;
Identify and communicate competitive and market issues to the SLT;
Improve and coordinate budget and forecasting processes;
Prepare cash flow forecasts managing liquidity and financial risks;
Assist with review of the 5-year business plan and provide input to the strategic planning process;
Assist with financial modelling and scenario planning analysis;
Liaise with the wider finance team to support any financial forecasting requirements and analysis;
Support the internal & external audit programme;
Ensure financial compliance with all matters relating to the FCA.
The Successful Applicant
As Senior FP&A Analyst you will be a qualified accountant (ACA/ACCA/CIMA) with experience working in or with the insurance sector. Part qualified accountants with strong experience in financial forecasting and budgeting processes will also be considered.
This role could appeal if you’re looking for your first move out of an accountancy practice, especially if you’ve had an insurance sector client base.
Ideally You Will Demonstrate
Strong communication skills and the ability to manage stakeholders at all levels;
Strength to work under pressure and adapt to change;
Self-starter with can do attitude;
Good understanding of P&L’s, cash flows and financial performance reporting;
Strong analytical and financial skills, with high degree of competency in financial modelling and Excel.
Please be aware that by applying through this job board your CV will be added to their database. Should you prefer, you can
apply
for this role direct via our website, artemisclarke.co.uk.
Artemis Clarke Ltd acts as an employment agency for permanent recruitment. By applying for this job, you accept the T&Cs, Privacy Policy and Disclaimers which can also be found on our website.
